\chapter{Hardware Implementation}

\section{Overview}
The Matter Jet Mk-30 requires a deeply integrated hardware architecture capable
of sustaining relativistic plasma confinement, petawatt-scale energy throughput,
cryogenic superconducting operation, ultra-high heat flux extraction, and
sovereign computational control. This chapter develops the complete hardware
implementation of the Mk-30 engine, including structural materials, magnetic
array construction, cooling systems, radiators, and FPGA interlock logic.

\section{Reaction Core Vessel Architecture}
The Reaction Core Vessel is constructed from:
\begin{itemize}
\item sintered silicon carbide (SiC) matrix,
\item continuous carbon fiber reinforcement,
\item 25~mm tungsten-rhenium (W-Re) internal liner,
\item vacuum isolation down to $10^{-9}$~Torr.
\end{itemize}

The vessel withstands:
\begin{itemize}
\item plasma temperatures $T_e = 1.42 \times 10^8$~K,
\item radiation energy density $u_{\text{rad}} = 4.1 \times 10^{25}$~J/m$^3$,
\item plasma pressure $p \approx 8.2 \times 10^{14}$~Pa.
\end{itemize}

The baryonic aerosol injection system delivers:
\[
\dot{m} = 12.98~\text{g/s},
\]
with piezoelectric micro-nozzles providing uniform mass distribution.

\section{Superconducting Magnet Array}
The superconducting magnet array consists of:
\begin{itemize}
\item REBCO high-temperature superconducting tapes,
\item stainless steel structural backing,
\item multi-stage liquid helium cryogenic jacket,
\item vacuum-insulated radiation shields.
\end{itemize}

The array generates:
\[
B_z = 1450~\text{T},
\qquad
\frac{\partial B}{\partial r} = 8.12 \times 10^3~\text{T/m}.
\]

The cryogenic envelope maintains:
\[
T_{\text{cryo}} = 4.2~\text{K}.
\]

\section{Magnetic Nozzle Construction}
The magnetic nozzle geometry includes:
\begin{itemize}
\item throat radius $r_0$,
\item confinement length $L$,
\item axial field $B_z$,
\item radial gradient $\partial B / \partial r$.
\end{itemize}

The nozzle is designed to:
