\section{GaIn Micro-Channel Cooling System}
The cooling system uses:
\begin{itemize}
\item eutectic gallium-indium (GaIn) coolant,
\item etched micro-channel heat exchangers,
\item SiC structural backing,
\item W-Re thermal interface layer.
\end{itemize}

The system absorbs:
\[
Q_{\text{absorbed}} = 5.0001 \times 10^{14}~\text{W},
\qquad
\Delta T = 412.4~\text{K}.
\]

The heat transfer coefficient is:
\[
h_{\text{channel}} \approx 1.8 \times 10^7~\text{W/m}^2\text{K}.
\]

\section{CNT Radiator Array}
The CNT radiator arrays operate at:
\[
T_{\text{eff}} \approx 5450~\text{K}.
\]

Radiated power:
\begin{equation}
P_{\text{rad}} = \epsilon \sigma A T_{\text{eff}}^4,
\end{equation}
with emissivity $\epsilon \approx 1$.

Peak emission:
\[
\lambda_{\text{peak}} \approx 531~\text{nm}.
\]

\section{FPGA Interlock Module}
The FPGA interlock enforces:
\begin{itemize}
\item power ceiling: $P < 20$~PW,
\item magnetic field floor: $B > 1000$~T,
\item thermal ceiling: $T < 10{,}000$~K,
\item cryptographic authentication.
\end{itemize}

The interlock module includes:
\begin{itemize}
\item containment coil relay,
\item fuel injector gate,
\item quench dump trigger,
\item deterministic state machine.
\end{itemize}

\section{SystemVerilog Interlock Logic}
The interlock logic is implemented in SystemVerilog:

\begin{verbatim}
module matter_jet_mk30_interlock (
    input  logic        clk,
    input  logic        reset_n,
    input  logic [63:0] power_telemetry_watts,
    input  logic [31:0] mag_field_tesla,
    input  logic [31:0] core_temp_kelvin,
    input  logic        crypto_auth_pass,
    output logic        containment_coil_enable,
    output logic        fuel_injector_gate,
    output logic        quench_dump_trigger
);
\end{verbatim}

The state machine transitions:
\[
\text{INIT} \rightarrow \text{RUN} \rightarrow \text{FAULT} \rightarrow \text{QUENCH}.
\]

Fault detection time:
\[
\tau_{\text{fault}} = 0.02~\mu\text{s}.
\]

